  "implementations": {
    "core": {
      "package": "core",
      "version": "2.5.0",
      "module": "pure/Map"
    },
    "plugin_custom": {
      "package": "plugin/pure-map",
      "version": "ABI 1",
      "comparison": "Motoko callback"
    },
    "plugin_static": {
      "package": "plugin/pure-map",
      "version": "ABI 1",
      "comparison": "native Nat64 ordering"
    }
  },
  "methodology": "Public function costs on exactly 1000/10000/100000 records by default. Same compiler, actor, boxed Nat64 keys, Nat values, lawful exact-key comparator, and shuffled distinct insertion order. Fresh canister per case/trial; map population, input arrays, output slots, prepared full snapshots and input builder iterators are outside timing. Construction rows separately measure fromIter/fromArray; other rows operate on populated maps. Points perform 32 calls with distinct spread keys; evolving updates retain first/middle/final roots. Contains/insert/delete/alter/update alternate hits and interleaved misses. Iterator creation retains4 cursors at 100k or 8 otherwise, consumed and exhausted only during validation. Iterator consumption measures creation plus full traversal and bounded order-sensitive hash/count, not output array copying. Seek rows create 4/8 cursors at positions spanning the complete rank range and consume 16 entries each. Find rows use the public Map.find with an ordered threshold predicate matching multiple entries where possible, first/middle/last/absent thresholds separately. Rank/select use 8 spread positions; split uses 3/4. Full scans/transforms/builders run once. Raw instruction/allocation/reclamation numbers include common loop, counter, retained-result assignment and checksum work; synchronous reclamation is reported, end-of-message GC excluded. Allocations are cumulative heap bytes, not retained live memory or RSS. Divide batch totals by operations_per_phase for costs per stated workload, not per iterator next. Core missing APIs use only the explicit public compositions documented per case; no complete map conversion or invented plugin API. Full snapshots compare Core root capture/replay via entries with plugin snapshot/replay metadata. Distinct builder inputs avoid Core 2.5 duplicate-size constructor defect. This callback round uses --fresh-per-phase true: every implementation gets a fresh canister for each workload/trial; implementations do not inherit prior measured phases or their correctness queries.",
  "correctness": "Checked-result query runs outside timing. It validates complete original maps after every phase, every old-value/Bool result, complete first/middle/final retained update versions and final outputs against an independent ordinal-slot oracle, sizes and plugin AVL invariants. Created cursors and snapshots are consumed in exact expected order and checked for repeatable exhaustion; consumed cursors retain their remaining suffix for exact validation. Timed traversal/folds use a bounded order-sensitive Nat64 checksum plus independent entry/callback count; expected checksum is generated from ordinal bindings outside timing. Split outputs are checked completely. Builder input cursors must be exhausted. Predicate search verifies the earliest matching key and exact predicate-call count. The query returns ok only after checks pass.",
